# Line-ending policy: LF in the repo, LF on checkout, machine-independent.
# Same policy as abandoned_cyber_city_zombies (proven there 2026-06):
# Radiant/GSC/linker all accept LF; Radiant re-saves CRLF on Windows and a
# commit normalizes back, so the repo never churns line endings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries - never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.flac binary
*.ogg binary
*.exr binary
*.tif binary
*.tiff binary
*.tga binary
*.dds binary
*.psd binary
*.iwi binary
*.xmodel_bin binary
*.xanim_bin binary
*.cast binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary
*.7z binary
*.rar binary

# Blender masters and the fan FBX sources ride Git LFS (docs/174, 2026-10-08): GitHub refuses any
# file over 100 MB (reference_two.blend is 128 MB) and every re-save of a master is a full copy.
# Free tier = 10 GiB storage + 10 GiB download / month; the 22 files were ~1.0 GB when added.
*.blend filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.fbx filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
